{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:36:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-22T17:06:24+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-22T17:06:28+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Hundru Falls\" \"wikimedia commons\" OR \"upload.wikimedia.org\" OR \"Patratu Valley\" OR \"Baidyanath Temple\" OR \"Parasnath\"\" returned the following summary:\nHundru Falls is a prominent waterfall located in the Ranchi district of Jharkhand, India, formed by the Subarnrekha River[1][2]. It is widely recognized as one of the highest waterfalls in the state, with a height of approximately 98 meters[1].\n\n### Wikimedia Commons Resources\n*   **Media Gallery:** There is an extensive category for \"Hundru Falls\" on Wikimedia Commons containing numerous photographs, including aerial views, landscape shots, and close-ups taken by various contributors[3].\n*   **Licensing:** Images on Wikimedia Commons are typically available under free licenses (such as Creative Commons Attribution or CC0), allowing for use provided that proper attribution—such as \"© [Author Name], CC BY [Version] via Wikimedia Commons\"—is included[4][3][2].\n\n### Nearby Attractions & Context\nHundru Falls is frequently visited in conjunction with other major tourist sites in Jharkhand:\n*   **Patratu Valley:** Known for its scenic winding roads and valley views, it is often listed as a notable attraction within traveling distance of the falls[5].\n*   **Parasnath:** Home to the Parasnath Hills and the Shikharji pilgrimage site, this area is a significant landmark in Jharkhand often associated with travel routes in the region[5][6].\n*   **Baidyanath Temple:** Located in Deoghar, this is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas and a major religious destination in the state, often appearing in regional travel itineraries alongside other landmarks[6].\n\nFor travelers, the region offers a mix of natural beauty, such as the nearby Jonha Falls and Dassam Falls, and significant cultural or religious sites like the various temples and hill stations surrounding Ranchi[5][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [wikimedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHGKxs0CCvMpYsQMWGbQw09ADX3WC65Tt0CXXXrnmv-fTXKFhf83K6TIXmuDluciWn9JmE30y1lnQhvhYPXlxd55rFuSGyY8fES1DuHbUnX1Qxu6Qc42quKugdWQGC1VrGLBnrLP-LgzbYpbx7FDRuqP9EaYwiD)\n[2] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFI4zTrf5m_085WC1mmf187m7GIc9TQeNTUYl_gFg-bBNCLTd501TQl9Y0p8KXZT8pzB-M4O-H9xhAfG7QOsNYuUfxjqIbAhDh2S6RotMUZyRkIlLI81KKprTCFpyM8GyPHQUOfWvzveExIVDaYGOiX33BwbCo3vWdvpweLQkndGzjBcIXuEYvRTOw80OKzxAbHdgF49mkHqfdiiOi4PVHa7MGvelWP)\n[3] [wikimedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHZ_WiNDZOJ-qHrMeVyWht4vDh2KaTfe6m8Cqkb8R8kGN_yjd3mXhm4Qt1U5U913a9xsIJFWF1Z3vBeL7OnAwImlr0auYXT6tfUIqIlvTMC80ypnGHbWU0Kpj_ujrIAVT9HZ9aQ5A0aflPFpnW1jA==)\n[4] [wikimedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_933fcPYheW6jYOe8B3s8VjoAwSTbvMxbBLVOgDB4-eiUJc5DUXI3fC4UTRY9kPFcztGa1wn-526bOVhWj-l4xmYKuWIW69Zay_GAhzfrUIMMZlD-dYzNcc0dzaMn5Hyh8rnBZvm3F09sY-swwLBaHX1XkkNMv_B3zCF9KnoF5UB0)\n[5] [holaciti.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEvDbF-hrK6hIH6hpjq_uiIDqMvy0AR76ahFCm1og5eElGn3Mbmwp3PD8bP6kem3VF4A-I-beaBjCBn73FwM3e_YIttEYlXO8hQ6cAQUzpNdYJqBQEQDtFakowbHSI9vUE80NyIi0N7C3BOJimnUtZ-IkjFcA==)\n[6] [rome2rio.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFNXoq6N8z_eO9Y5UMMCSIG9JHCkPj5CirA0V5-Ha8txprjs1iS_St2Ac2j0TNi2m6T_nNhn_8rC8ZfACxpNUPO95J3ta9KhjIDkdADG5i_dzNxiXBAjuNRn8nTEVX7j9a87hNI7I3tP38J5XPbZNQ=)"}
