{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:36:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-22T17:06:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-22T17:06:51+05:30\nThe search for \"site:en.wikipedia.org \"Hundru Falls\" OR \"Jonha Falls\" OR \"Dassam Falls\" OR \"Patratu Valley\" OR \"Baidyanath Temple\" OR \"Parasnath\" OR \"Betla National Park\" OR \"Netarhat\" OR \"Lodh Falls\" OR \"Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary\" OR \"Tagore Hill\" OR \"Maithon Dam\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe requested sites are all notable tourist and geographical locations within the Indian state of Jharkhand, as documented on Wikipedia:\n\n*   **Waterfalls:**\n    *   [Hundru Falls](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hundru_Falls): A popular waterfall on the Subarnarekha River in Ranchi District[1][2].\n    *   [Jonha Falls](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonha_Falls): Also known as Gautamdhara Falls, located in Ranchi district[3].\n    *   [Dassam Falls](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dassam_Falls): A waterfall on the Kanchi River near Taimara village in Ranchi district[4].\n    *   [Lodh Falls](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lodh_Falls): The highest waterfall in Jharkhand, located on the Burha River in Latehar district[5][6].\n\n*   **Nature & Landscapes:**\n    *   [Patratu Valley](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patratu): Known for its scenic, winding roads through forested hills in the Ramgarh district[7][8].\n    *   [Betla National Park](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betla_National_Park): A prominent national park and tiger reserve spanning Latehar and Palamu districts[9][10].\n    *   [Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalma_Wildlife_Sanctuary): A sanctuary known for its Indian elephant population, located in East Singhbhum and Saraikela Kharsawan districts[11].\n    *   [Netarhat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netarhat): A hill station in Latehar district, famously referred to as the \"Queen of Chotanagpur\"[12][13].\n    *   [Tagore Hill](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagore_Hill): Also known as Morabadi Hill, located in Ranchi and associated with Rabindranath Tagore[14].\n\n*   **Religious & Engineering Landmarks:**\n    *   [Baidyanath Temple](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baidyanath_Temple): A major Hindu temple in Deoghar, recognized as one of the twelve Jyotirlingas[15][16].\n    *   [Parasnath](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parasnath): A major Jain pilgrimage site (Shikharji) and the highest mountain peak in Jharkhand[17][18].\n    *   [Maithon Dam](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maithon_Dam): A major dam built on the Barakar River in the Dhanbad district, known for its underground power station[19].\n\nSources:\n[1] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG9ph9RykkUim9jdtzcbGjZwtIHQ3ulKU2v3YY2ddG3iC9rVi0SPXA2_A1c8LrAkb0FQ_-ZPBRYWzwSLRNyLdQrVB2QSe-f6Odo9lue7LsrL_ADYVQW-VPpehiR7PbKcw==)\n[2] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG9ph9RykkUim9jdtzcbGjZwtIHQ3ulKU2v3YY2ddG3iC9rVi0SPXA2_A1c8LrAkb0FQ_-ZPBRYWzwSLRNyLdQrVB2QSe-f6Odo9lue7LsrL_ADYVQW-VPpehiR7PbKcw==)\n[3] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCn-8pm7brvkrDuHlumTN_AT9Y9j16Jd3H44lIRfIkJn9SxDS6iVkSTfwjR2mrR3HozE3hul1aL0UgDe5z3Mcu7qO47g3E8nXnMMyj_RHPfDqwH5AM1_WBv_UQJlYn)\n[4] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFvy27jRW4G6lYb93D_3NGJSBKkRBvW4UcOykSgVVxqxMZ14Vp_DGNpP6xSarqygKT8jLGwRweA1g2JVm_py6W34Al2XLMr4J_HLGK8hSroHmncyCL9RPiRpn3_plzY8Q==)\n[5] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFywXbVZ5yNj97Ejcnpphs_OQkxOTh1HFyHl2i5yVsBN9L_81m0NAj14cYHI2Si3gBFrgiCylxTW_cbvaRx-QwdBSM_48_xlbzZs_vVKTlglsCTeWSAgQcypLJdqWE=)\n[6] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGVTNqgLrBNGml1duSFM8zL1Ax4QUX1LtUUrafCZBQmwby3OWi2KAlx9Zal0rKuZZgRhjZp1WWkJh4OOujmzWSSlYEunbmi6OEsxwavxp-eSCFP